on" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13960038/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-8331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-8331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}ky \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-8331" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "575f912e44c38b296f556ff9695377cdf795d1ce07ad53a6b7cbc672ec0dd20b"} {"question" "q-8331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-8331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-8331" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} & =18{v}_{1}+3{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2} \\\\  & =18({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =18(0)+3{v}_{1} \\\\  & =3{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=T(3{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}) & =3T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =3[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(21{v}_{1}+18{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "575f912e44c38b296f556ff9695377cdf795d1ce07ad53a6b7cbc672ec0dd20b"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}108 \\\\ -72 \\\\ 60\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ -18 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}162 \\\\ -108 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+3{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+3T({v}_{2}) \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "575f912e44c38b296f556ff9695377cdf795d1ce07ad53a6b7cbc672ec0dd20b"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-37898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, then find $\\,T({v}_{1}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kv+hw)=T(kv)+T(hw)=kT(v)+hT(w)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3{v}_{1}+7{v}_{2}) & =3T({v}_{1})+7T({v}_{2}) \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =3T({v}_{1})+7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ 3T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "575f912e44c38b296f556ff9695377cdf795d1ce07ad53a6b7cbc672ec0dd20b"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74775" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a linear transformation $\\,T\\,.$ If $\\,{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0\\,$ and $\\,T({v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\,$, find $\\,T(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}+13{v}_{2}-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13(0)-5{v}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{v}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2})=T(-5{v}_{2}).\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{2}) \\\\  & =-5[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(13{v}_{1}+8{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "575f912e44c38b296f556ff9695377cdf795d1ce07ad53a6b7cbc672ec0dd20b"} {"question" "q-74780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715af"} {"question" "q-74780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-40 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 45\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-64 \\\\ 32 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}40 \\\\ -20 \\\\ -45\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}64 \\\\ -32 \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067344/state.json" "file_sha256" "0751fff2314bd52dff1552ec65f4f0c3df5e7fb44882ac8a06a081c6502715